ID: vr-63
Title: Attribute and bound a complete live head's memory cost

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Post-M1 measured resource ownership
Dependencies: vr-61

Purpose:
  Explain and, where causal evidence supports it, reduce the full warm
  Claire/Hazel/Electron process tree's substantial private committed memory.

Tasks:
  Attribute host, voice worker, Electron main/renderer/GPU/helper costs.
  Distinguish model, current speech, CPU/GPU geometry and Chromium allocations.
  Compare bounded post-speech settling/replacement/cancellation cycles.
  Fix only demonstrated avoidable retention and prove selected-only ownership.

Acceptance criteria:
  Use private commit, unique/working-set and GPU measurements with correct names.
  Retain comparable before/after scenarios and explicit shared-process limits.
  Do not call ordinary latest-clip/cache retention a leak without evidence.
  Preserve current quality, cancellation, audio-clock behavior and RAM-only data.
  Any saving must be measured over complete process trees, not engine-only numbers.

Completion evidence:
  .local\qualification\live-use-01\receipt.json: same eight-process tree throughout.
    Mean private commit 887.04MiB before speech, peak 963.82MiB during generation,
    and mean 940.72MiB over the eight-second post-speech window.
    This is not unique physical RAM, a proved leak, or a controlled steady-state
    off/on comparison. Shared manager and unrelated apps are excluded.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Opened from real session observation at the owner's request;
    component attribution and further memory improvement remain planned.
